  "description": "<p>South Seattle College was founded in 1969 in West Seattle, Washington. It is a part of the network of Seattle colleges in the Seattle college district: North Seattle College, Seattle Central College, and South Seattle College. Students can complete the first two years of a bachelor's degree program and get a Bachelor of Applied Science degree.</p><p>Around 500 international students represent approximately 50 countries on campus at South Seattle College. The College empowers students to be able to train for rewarding careers in a variety of professional/technical programs.</p><h2>What is the South Seattle College acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The South Seattle College acceptance rate is 100%.</p> <p> The South Seattle College Fitness Center is open for student use and contains a fully equipped gym offering various fitness equipment and classes. The Student Centre has a cafeteria, lounge areas, meeting rooms, a game room, and a student government office. The South Seattle College Performing Arts Center features a 500-seat theater, dance studio, and music practice rooms.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Student life is varied, and students feel the College cares about their well-being. From the Seattle Chinese Garden to the Art Gallery, students feel intellectually and emotionally stimulated when they study at South Seattle College. Meaningful services, activities and communications that build community are available at South Seattle College.</p>",
