      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>South Seattle College was founded in 1969 in West Seattle, Washington. It is a part of the network of Seattle colleges in the Seattle college district: North Seattle College, Seattle Central College, and South Seattle College. Students can complete the first two years of a bachelor's degree program and get a Bachelor of Applied Science degree.</p><p>Around 500 international students represent approximately 50 countries on campus at South Seattle College. The College empowers students to be able to train for rewarding careers in a variety of professional/technical programs.</p>",
